Judeikis"},"message":"Edges: don''t re-mint a join token during registration\n\nRegistering an agent takes two writes by two different writers: the hub\nclears status.joinToken with a MergePatch, and the lifecycle reconciler\nmarks the edge Registered afterwards. Between them the edge has a token\nhash, no plaintext token, and no Registered=True -- which is exactly the\nstate the token controller treated as \"needs a token\".\n\nSo clearing the token was itself the trigger to regenerate it. The\nreplacement overwrote JoinTokenHash with the digest of a token nobody\nholds, and the hub''s follow-up clear then destroyed that token''s\nplaintext too. The agent in the field, still holding the token it\nenrolled with, was refused on every reconnect from then on -- observed\nas an edge that connects once and never comes back after its agent\nrestarts.\n\nDon''t mint when a hash is already present: a hash with no plaintext\nmeans a token was issued and an agent enrolled with it. Rotation stays\nexplicit through AnnotationRegenerateJoinToken, which is handled before\nthis check.\n\nThe guard moves into needsJoinToken so the window it closes can be\ndocumented and tested without a multicluster manager.","tree":{"sha":"c3b36350a7b5252b77903db82f11669907313a2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/c3b36350a7b5252b77903db82f11669907313a2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/1d9cbe223f3c56329a82666760918f5b8e43c935","verification":{"payload":"tree c3b36350a7b5252b77903db82f11669907313a2e\nparent 7772b5b9eb0dd6a9cd6dd4e8fd284103959bd529\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1791459637 +0300\ncommitter Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1791459637 +0300\n\nEdges: don''t re-mint a join token during registration\n\nRegistering an agent takes two writes by two different writers: the hub\nclears status.joinToken with a MergePatch, and the lifecycle reconciler\nmarks the edge Registered afterwards. Between them the edge has a token\nhash, no plaintext token, and no Registered=True -- which is exactly the\nstate the token controller treated as \"needs a token\".\n\nSo clearing the token was itself the trigger to regenerate it. The\nreplacement overwrote JoinTokenHash with the digest of a token nobody\nholds, and the hub''s follow-up clear then destroyed that token''s\nplaintext too. The agent in the field, still holding the token it\nenrolled with, was refused on every reconnect from then on -- observed\nas an edge that connects once and never comes back after its agent\nrestarts.\n\nDon''t mint when a hash is already present: a hash with no plaintext\nmeans a token was issued and an agent enrolled with it. Rotation stays\nexplicit through AnnotationRegenerateJoinToken, which is handled before\nthis check.\n\nThe guard moves into needsJoinToken so the window it closes can be\ndocumented and tested without a multicluster manager.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEMtV72CeF+eCb0QAlQ+sIBvLbYkcFAmrHgTUbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEEPrCAby22JHqi8QAKU1gyFP/i4Sz4Owcv2R\nDxUzkvXsroD5mGkaTg9Y9hyYiaIeIFX0zEUzMhNUdPvfo02+fDXUqpDJ/hg+0tsU\n/jzyRDH8byhUUASwxdv/3STVvp+sPOBeANBSYd52d0c1JlSG6MJa3esGx3JG9+Xi\nrqNwlQMp+XAmKB9jWgupjBrnjKkL5zJ/glJhvq6wjkeMaqyrKwe0TvSBnOQNFTWz\nwDCnSo/lBNZtjVfQJfdn7r1abE9SQzt90mgjE6gTQuEMbqs/SrkcU3xtXOQ+//4l\nbPVyoYk4nQzlyw0iq/pW0NqH17zZWKqwogb3+x0gUtj6c54Y/0x0AG+j12CiD9qX\nHmEquQ+t7Ug3DgJ4c+d7fLSkpyy/Ais+/ADkDgBKp7XM4gdwt1pKtRO4LQ08D4lD\n3iHN5tyDUosO3frAQ9ZrmC/yqv+Fv8WZbPNmw2PQIrVnxSHxsCWgqqiqJWAngDJo\ngKc80hYP67PLMPhowUvQjNV/C27s8f6EBS6WYK7WPPCMSorpx0lqi0xtQ1EnnNfo\nhc6LkhtSqlMZO2zHbPP5mJLsqqrIWs76V8s7xl8x2cJovH5T5i8+W+B0LAQ31Xti\nPzcgQpXaQ6JhgtahS9kgQ/Dffkk/a3jvxAr5QDkJDmzGC15qasWkFI1OobZK0xwC\nrPshu9+WmL5uKu5OVJYMKYWW\n=/MpD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T11:40:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","event