69)\n\n* Provider contract hardenining\n\n* extend providers sdk with serve\n\n* rework apiexport cross-claims\n\n* fix duplicate hash\n\n* Rework provider integrations\n\n* e2e test\n\n* Fix Ci\n\n* fix more CI\n\n* Fix broken features","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsCwxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQEIQADIyVYnMNqSzhscMy1jIqiul\n4hYTs3weSUUNU9zlEPgxx8rzwOplJ3H7cVB0w3TYxZs8UEghWYscw/W3JhsmN/pI\nV1geVWS12+wQMma7LGKSft69DI+vAHx9NF6ht4e7th3tYxpVFBe21zB0lafAOA5N\nc0yx3bI24DBsia32wqqHdKH0oJgpuxb+FFjAy1n03Wb1zp4iZ8eJ2AtPnQX2Fq4Z\nouWvA+s29X+F/Za7oZ6T/6Ivnnxvztcn9J016GmaKCQQTvFhQl3jC4JPcFoMNUnF\n3lJ3DdORGvw/Tyof7uTa20r+FBb6YFrTDO4PsBBg6I02J9rWiFHjnPYwHs8w2QQJ\nWlkkw7nnRPzRrcdNYVL6rMMLVTCCD3XLVxcqgQMzPLmNoP7rQcGmas9hxDxorjST\nUKECieHV9kX7RSfQFXU6YBC0v0EuSMDmZha/YdOo/3cCXN5Gl0Ao/8EYtr0+t8YP\nwq6htZ/ZcgJPhJCrJ8PPKKjtwxiiUjALGocD3+x3HfLGX77hwzJoVEErM6Qc2dfz\nQ9VVcYwe61gCqDoGpK0H/yUT/eQzVXsaiwsx5tjy0uQpJVTN6gBRUtyGApWbPvlp\nJh+KvJsl6QbNyfcIrHJNKI5yY8deTvKLihBPNCCCUWW7Kc0nKCFAHrGkcpXffSsb\n7kQOSFV44jCx4HVNmSti\n=9iWl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:55:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/7691b50fce759090a102881ecc625676d732a794","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKDc2OTFiNTBmY2U3NTkwOTBhMTAyODgxZWNjNjI1Njc2ZDczMmE3OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811","sha":"b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811"}],"sha":"7691b50fce759090a102881ecc625676d732a794","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/7691b50fce759090a102881ecc625676d732a794"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T13:11:10Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T13:11:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Report providers with no consumers as ready, not unready (#768)\n\nkcp publishes a shard''s virtual-workspace URL into an\nAPIExportEndpointSlice only once the export has a consumer there. An\nempty slice therefore means no workspace has enabled the provider yet,\nbut both vwhealth''s probe and apiexportprovider.Provider.Check reported\nit as unready. The catalog then showed every freshly installed provider\nas \"Not ready\", which is what stops anyone from enabling it.\n\nTreat an empty slice as idle: vwhealth gains ErrNoEndpoints and\nReadiness.Idle, /readyz answers 200 with a detail, and Provider.Check\nreturns ready. Unreachable published endpoints, failing watchers and\nunstarted or stopped providers still report unready.","tree":{"sha":"a6a3ca2f13b7e8dcc6df08657c4762fa26668391","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/a6a3ca2f13b7e8dcc6df08657c4762fa26668391"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811","verification":{"payload":"tree a6a3ca2f13b7e8dcc6df08657c4762fa26668391\nparent c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789823470 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789823470 +0300\n\nReport providers with no consumers as ready, not unready (#768)\n\nkcp publishes a shard''s virtual-workspace URL into an\nAPIExportEndpointSlice only once the export has a consumer there. An\nempty slice therefore means no workspace has enabled the provider yet,\nbut both vwhealth''s probe and apiexportprovider.Provider.Check reported\nit as unready. The catalog then showed every freshly installed provider\nas \"Not ready\", which is what stops anyone from enabling it.\n\nTreat an empty slice as idle: vwhealth gains ErrNoEndpoints and\nReadiness.Idle, /readyz answers 200 with a detail, and Provider.Check\nreturns ready. Unreachable published endpoints, failing watchers and\nunstarted or stopped providers still report unready.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqronuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/q4QAHG3FctwZUtuCcT+DyCoZomf\nKnEXe1++AzOB/xMpZqojyRh/6mj9CcggrpGr2G7S1Y0ENtDanCtUaX5APaNtvWqs\niEB9Kl7gwgr8ra/52S6VNc694DOb3YfhT9QLjtf/Dnfyt6Ha+LzmGThoyHhGCveA\naig+jYzFvCYag/QP/ZgjCwexz+v5azVcR/6b0DEk4hUkOWcpakVf/OPafTts7Pm5\nEVdOQXtahcskpYfq8grQinegjhSQXU5kIrV6dLUMavkSb9XLjChxbpbHj7iIHUW4\nRflX14DRFWeOmrVC/wZePBGDkMjdoqKpWai+KztX22SphwfvCvPPIE4uJt8loBTP\nPrvOvWzEMRJeGVHA/Yqghrhmqd5ZLe/tsJyQZ+syf6nOzGfo46xJFAqZQHZ6m9v0\nH0G/avhljO8Ld8RmZ81jNX1zMvtPtG1FWg/RjqDcHLubROtIXkEjZMfb6S8t5EF0\nVvW97NCgKhZXylOhhnvwdDybnG/b+bOYwhaAQRI60P0DbtV40SkkdDBANxGlK502\nkLdLn8OtFJzwMwf0ot2fBqg1IT0zLjItqR6ylRP13pF4symYwLBl6GvdmX9jRH6J\nXdxRj1vbdADeLs74Y8oOwPToRP77wXlOho9PnuptXzIPSo5oEYHO7oS6LJNV5M3I\n29tXXNedWaNXdVYSq0Bk\n=Bg47\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T13:11:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKGIxZTliNWU2YmE1Y2YyMTU5Nzc5NWFjY2I4YzJhNWZiMDQyNGY4MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711","sha":"c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711"}],"sha":"b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/b1e9b5e6ba5cf21597795accb8c2a5fb0424f811"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:36:02Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:36:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers (#766)\n\n* Refresh runner sources from origin and harden add-on permissions\n\nThe local runner now refreshes a source checkout from its own origin when\nan approved commit is missing (a base branch that moved on after a merge),\nusing the operator''s Git credentials with hooks disabled, and only then\nserves the isolated task clone from it. fetchRemoteURL becomes the\nfallback for sources without a usable origin. The add-on supervisor\nreclaims orphaned children on unix, linux and bsd hosts.\n\nEdge add-ons gain permissionMode and allowedTools so a coding runner can\nbe pinned to acceptEdits with an explicit shell allow list; CRDs and\nschemas are regenerated. The code provider''s GitHub backend treats only a\nmerged pull request as merge proof and verifies runner snapshot commits\nheader by header. App Studio''s assistant permission check pauses\npromote_project and hydrate_workspace in every approval mode short of\nNever.\n\n* Drive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers\n\nEvery provider polled internal platform state on a timer somewhere:\nreconcilers requeueing every 10 to 60 seconds to re-read objects they\ncould watch, HTTP handlers owning lifecycle state a reconciler also\nwrote, and one provider with no reconcilers at all. Only external\nsystems (GitHub, LLM APIs, helm, edge devices over the tunnel) should be\npolled; everything else now converges on watches.\n\nagents: a leader-elected multicluster-runtime manager on the agents\nAPIExport runs Schedule, Connection and Agent reconcilers in place of the\n30s CR scan. Schedule fires via RequeueAfter and a conflict-checked\nstatus claim; Connection owns Slack/Telegram secret repair, OAuth refresh\nat expiry and Discord session state, with a Secret watch. Runs stay in\nPostgres by design; cancellation is durable through a cancel_requested\ncolumn the engine checks before every model round and tool call, and\nevery submit path persists a Pending row before enqueueing.\n\nedges: the lifecycle reconciler is the single writer of Edge\nconnected/phase/lastHeartbeatTime, derived from the tunnel-registry\nLease and triggered by a Lease watch and connection-manager events, so\nit is correct at any replica count. The tunnel handler and the\nagent-side reporter no longer write those fields. The addon reconciler\nwatches its token Secret; the scheduler drops its unconditional 30s\nrequeue.\n\ninfrastructure: the Instance reconciler watches runtime-cluster CRs\n(registered per Template GVR), Templates and tenant Secrets instead of\n10s/60s/3s requeues; runtime CRs carry cluster and instance annotations\nso events map back. The Template reconciler watches RGDs so kro\nrejection surfaces in BackendReady.\n\napp-studio: Project and Studio reconcilers watch Repository,\nRepositoryCommit and Instance objects through each workspace''s own\nbindings; the in-memory pending-commit map becomes a Project annotation\nbacked by a workspace ledger; sandbox readiness and deletion use a single\nwatch; Session status is signalled by the supervisor on turn transitions\ninstead of a 30s Postgres poll.\n\ncode: MCP tools wait on a watch instead of a 1s GET loop; Collaborator\nrequeues while a GitHub invitation is pending.\n\nkuery: KubernetesClusters are watched per workspace through the\nworkspace''s own edges binding; the 20s requeue remains only as the Lease\nheartbeat.\n\nNo cross-provider permission claims were added: they pin one identity\nhash and break when an org self-hosts a provider (see ed0766f8).\n\n* update agent.md\n\n* refrence in providers\n\n* Fix CI: hydrate test race, agents image build, containerd advisory\n\nThe hydrate tool test read its sync-action record while the scheduled\nsync goroutine was still appending to it; the record is now guarded and\nthe test waits for the first call. The agents image build copied an\nexplicit directory list that predates the controllers, scheme and\ninternal packages, so it now copies the whole module like the code\nprovider. containerd moves to 1.7.35 in the root and edges modules for\nGO-2026-6444, which the vulnerability gate started reporting on\n2026-09-16.","tree":{"sha":"647e02a23c0d6444e453e380e767b090e496091e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/647e02a23c0d6444e453e380e767b090e496091e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711","verification":{"payload":"tree 647e02a23c0d6444e453e380e767b090e496091e\nparent 027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789760162 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789760162 +0300\n\nDrive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers (#766)\n\n* Refresh runner sources from origin and harden add-on permissions\n\nThe local runner now refreshes a source checkout from its own origin when\nan approved commit is missing (a base branch that moved on after a merge),\nusing the operator''s Git credentials with hooks disabled, and only then\nserves the isolated task clone from it. fetchRemoteURL becomes the\nfallback for sources without a usable origin. The add-on supervisor\nreclaims orphaned children on unix, linux and bsd hosts.\n\nEdge add-ons gain permissionMode and allowedTools so a coding runner can\nbe pinned to acceptEdits with an explicit shell allow list; CRDs and\nschemas are regenerated. The code provider''s GitHub backend treats only a\nmerged pull request as merge proof and verifies runner snapshot commits\nheader by header. App Studio''s assistant permission check pauses\npromote_project and hydrate_workspace in every approval mode short of\nNever.\n\n* Drive provider flows with reconcilers and watches instead of timers\n\nEvery provider polled internal platform state on a timer somewhere:\nreconcilers requeueing every 10 to 60 seconds to re-read objects they\ncould watch, HTTP handlers owning lifecycle state a reconciler also\nwrote, and one provider with no reconcilers at all. Only external\nsystems (GitHub, LLM APIs, helm, edge devices over the tunnel) should be\npolled; everything else now converges on watches.\n\nagents: a leader-elected multicluster-runtime manager on the agents\nAPIExport runs Schedule, Connection and Agent reconcilers in place of the\n30s CR scan. Schedule fires via RequeueAfter and a conflict-checked\nstatus claim; Connection owns Slack/Telegram secret repair, OAuth refresh\nat expiry and Discord session state, with a Secret watch. Runs stay in\nPostgres by design; cancellation is durable through a cancel_requested\ncolumn the engine checks before every model round and tool call, and\nevery submit path persists a Pending row before enqueueing.\n\nedges: the lifecycle reconciler is the single writer of Edge\nconnected/phase/lastHeartbeatTime, derived from the tunnel-registry\nLease and triggered by a Lease watch and connection-manager events, so\nit is correct at any replica count. The tunnel handler and the\nagent-side reporter no longer write those fields. The addon reconciler\nwatches its token Secret; the scheduler drops its unconditional 30s\nrequeue.\n\ninfrastructure: the Instance reconciler watches runtime-cluster CRs\n(registered per Template GVR), Templates and tenant Secrets instead of\n10s/60s/3s requeues; runtime CRs carry cluster and instance annotations\nso events map back. The Template reconciler watches RGDs so kro\nrejection surfaces in BackendReady.\n\napp-studio: Project and Studio reconcilers watch Repository,\nRepositoryCommit and Instance objects through each workspace''s own\nbindings; the in-memory pending-commit map becomes a Project annotation\nbacked by a workspace ledger; sandbox readiness and deletion use a single\nwatch; Session status is signalled by the supervisor on turn transitions\ninstead of a 30s Postgres poll.\n\ncode: MCP tools wait on a watch instead of a 1s GET loop; Collaborator\nrequeues while a GitHub invitation is pending.\n\nkuery: KubernetesClusters are watched per workspace through the\nworkspace''s own edges binding; the 20s requeue remains only as the Lease\nheartbeat.\n\nNo cross-provider permission claims were added: they pin one identity\nhash and break when an org self-hosts a provider (see ed0766f8).\n\n* update agent.md\n\n* refrence in providers\n\n* Fix CI: hydrate test race, agents image build, containerd advisory\n\nThe hydrate tool test read its sync-action record while the scheduled\nsync goroutine was still appending to it; the record is now guarded and\nthe test waits for the first call. The agents image build copied an\nexplicit directory list that predates the controllers, scheme and\ninternal packages, so it now copies the whole module like the code\nprovider. containerd moves to 1.7.35 in the root and edges modules for\nGO-2026-6444, which the vulnerability gate started reporting on\n2026-09-16.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZKiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe8oQAIBvftjYDSRcEgcbH+cS3Uvj\n1VsUSgw9mOAbN0i3pB91dUCET0b1hvV2uEcZllX/hCOZvHJfTWkOYjVcBwta+A2P\nHlmvEJvD7TFePMNeWw/Sfb856eYhY9EnkVKktDXPztUF8wRcdkv/IA6VzMZW8HOu\npsB/e4zJYztk1/PEKLdnk8mfxmImAXzClZbdWNYvWjEEZoioMcMjLQmGeUcl/1/x\naH5sVgCnm3UJIrnae8pmamacKbqhkKy9sJvF/Oqf1hY2DeoHKssJiDHnwNVVqokW\nt0u+zCHpCT/Z4Oe83iSQQOE7aKTR+5BGTCUNrYZZhlnrfjO4g+uRuDOw2g9g4eEF\ngARaNl3u0KO6/hpLB9nVzkIbMHMWp9DxYBaS1g4ha/XZFARMh8zJJ7bN1AFPIY8H\nAArkKEwyvFPrTrh3bc84H+dNM8BgOHxuyK9JXwEI8k3z3eoKjxBwDklE3ootrEDO\nDU5EMMCkSzhofmlBcNXVw4OSeKY5MYSmwGHpAN/RDmCidVdTRz8Hpxx+yuXimZCE\nfYJVvbAtODy67/gT9/vfppq8ac16QMBpaRCiErUc9RniYLyQNH3+CYPjRUuaqUsX\nMmazmCvDSywF43xUIWseGFgw7XV2AypfRsHRrizmTWVYsF0nhE/wofQPnETapUxh\nv54104zn5DhRkMTvWelz\n=dX49\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T19:36:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKGM2NjcwOTU2MDZjMWY4NjdmNzI2YTQyZTlkYjBkZjY4YTZjZDM3MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895","sha":"027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895"}],"sha":"c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c667095606c1f867f726a42e9db0df68a6cd3711"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:20:04Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:20:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Edge add-on control plane with a managed coding runner, plus provider fixes (#765)\n\n* Relay kcp discovery roots and harden external provider Tilt wiring\n\nThe hub only relayed /api/ and /apis/ prefixes, so the bare /api and /apis\ndiscovery roots 404ed for ServiceAccount callers. client-go''s REST mapper\nlists API groups from them first, so a provider running a controller-runtime\nmanager behind the hub could not start.\n\nExternal providers in the embedded Tilt stack now get host port-forwards with\nCatalogEntry URLs the host hub can reach, a kcp loopback bridge for the\n127.0.0.1:6443 virtual-workspace URLs embedded kcp advertises, and the dev\nserving certificate as a hub CA. They are skipped with a warning when they\nlack local setup. The api-only passthrough is gone: the provider library no\nlonger has it.\n\n* Let templates that handle a missing manifest sync without one\n\nThe development sync rejected any node component without a root package.json,\nbut simple-webapp''s start command tests for the file and falls back to\nnpx vite. A static index.html project was refused by a sandbox that can run\nit. Skip the manifest check when the start command itself tests for it.\n\n* Refresh expiring GitHub OAuth tokens and re-validate connections\n\nA GitHub OAuth App with token expiration issues 8h access tokens plus a\nsingle-use refresh token. The connect flow kept only the access token, so\nevery such Connection died after eight hours while still reporting Validated.\n\nThe callback now returns the refresh token and expiry, the portal stores them\nnext to the token, and every credential read renews an expiring token with\nthe app''s refresh grant, writing the rotated pair back under a\nresourceVersion precondition. Connections are also re-validated every 15\nminutes, so a token the host revoked stops reading as valid.\n\n* Package the runner for Linux and share the acceptance setup script\n\npackage.py takes the target OS, so make package-runner-linux produces\nrailgrid-runner-linux-<arch> archives alongside the macOS ones. The\nacceptance fixture script is no longer macOS-specific and is renamed to\nsetup.sh.\n\n* Add an edge add-on control plane with a managed coding runner\n\nThe edge agent can now materialize add-on services declared in the tenant\nworkspace, following the existing declare -> materialize -> report loop\ninstead of an imperative hub-to-agent channel.\n\n- New Addon API (edges.railgrid.ai): spec.edgeRef, type runner, and the runner\n  configuration, with Allowed/Configured/Running/Published conditions.\n- Two keys are required: the tenant creates the Addon AND the machine owner\n  started the agent with --allow-addon (default none). Edges report\n  status.allowedAddons; the provider publishes the runner Service only after\n  the agent reports Allowed=True. MCPServer tokens never get addons.\n- The agent supervises the child as a non-root account (--addon-user when the\n  agent is root), with an environment built from scratch, process-group\n  termination, restart backoff and owner-only, symlink-hardened state.\n- railgrid runner run embeds the runner in the main binary, which is what the\n  agent starts.\n- Claude Code is a second runner harness next to Codex: headless stream-json\n  turns with resume, customization and MCP disabled, and the credential read\n  from an owner-only file, injected only into the harness process and redacted\n  from events. Addons choose it with spec.runner.harness.\n\nThe dev server edge allows the runner add-on (DEV_EDGE_ALLOW_ADDONS), and the\ndev serving certificate covers host.docker.internal so provider pods can\nverify the host hub.","tree":{"sha":"ab39555180cc3899ab0460145141b39740bc1208","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/ab39555180cc3899ab0460145141b39740bc1208"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/027c21c8c56590bd98c4e40fd581aae97e688895","verification":{"payload":"tree ab39555180cc3899ab0460145141b39740bc1208\nparent d002fd91629ab4f6bbd93a4d6e0758f3e84d4758\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789669204 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789669204 +0300\n\nEdge add-on control plane with a managed coding runner, plus provider fixes (#765)\n\n* Relay kcp discovery roots and harden external provider Tilt wiring\n\nThe hub only relayed /api/ and /apis/ prefixes, so the bare /api and /apis\ndiscovery roots 404ed for ServiceAccount callers. client-go''s REST mapper\nlists API groups from them first, so a provider running a controller-runtime\nmanager behind the hub could not start.\n\nExternal providers in the embedded Tilt stack now get host port-forwards with\nCatalogEntry URLs the host hub can reach, a kcp loopback bridge for the\n127.0.0.1:6443 virtual-workspace URLs embedded kcp advertises, and the dev\nserving certificate as a hub CA. They are skipped with a warning when they\nlack local setup. The api-only passthrough is gone: the provider library no\nlonger has it.\n\n* Let templates that handle a missing manifest sync without one\n\nThe development sync rejected any node component without a root package.json,\nbut simple-webapp''s start command tests for the file and falls back to\nnpx vite. A static index.html project was refused by a sandbox that can run\nit. Skip the manifest check when the start command itself tests for it.\n\n* Refresh expiring GitHub OAuth tokens and re-validate connections\n\nA GitHub OAuth App with token expiration issues 8h access tokens plus a\nsingle-use refresh token. The connect flow kept only the access token, so\nevery such Connection died after eight hours while still reporting Validated.\n\nThe callback now returns the refresh token and expiry, the portal stores them\nnext to the token, and every credential read renews an expiring token with\nthe app''s refresh grant, writing the rotated pair back under a\nresourceVersion precondition. Connections are also re-validated every 15\nminutes, so a token the host revoked stops reading as valid.\n\n* Package the runner for Linux and share the acceptance setup script\n\npackage.py takes the target OS, so make package-runner-linux produces\nrailgrid-runner-linux-<arch> archives alongside the macOS ones. The\nacceptance fixture script is no longer macOS-specific and is renamed to\nsetup.sh.\n\n* Add an edge add-on control plane with a managed coding runner\n\nThe edge agent can now materialize add-on services declared in the tenant\nworkspace, following the existing declare -> materialize -> report loop\ninstead of an imperative hub-to-agent channel.\n\n- New Addon API (edges.railgrid.ai): spec.edgeRef, type runner, and the runner\n  configuration, with Allowed/Configured/Running/Published conditions.\n- Two keys are required: the tenant creates the Addon AND the machine owner\n  started the agent with --allow-addon (default none). Edges report\n  status.allowedAddons; the provider publishes the runner Service only after\n  the agent reports Allowed=True. MCPServer tokens never get addons.\n- The agent supervises the child as a non-root account (--addon-user when the\n  agent is root), with an environment built from scratch, process-group\n  termination, restart backoff and owner-only, symlink-hardened state.\n- railgrid runner run embeds the runner in the main binary, which is what the\n  agent starts.\n- Claude Code is a second runner harness next to Codex: headless stream-json\n  turns with resume, customization and MCP disabled, and the credential read\n  from an owner-only file, injected only into the harness process and redacted\n  from events. Addons choose it with spec.runner.harness.\n\nThe dev server edge allows the runner add-on (DEV_EDGE_ALLOW_ADDONS), and the\ndev serving certificate covers host.docker.internal so provider pods can\nverify the host hub.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrC9UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJLgQAKDkcO3l/TSLxToAbjNnsfEE\nMJdRuKOSX+rGlkml7RiVX+O8NbSOmiZSndJDVxCajkK8aa+G8CGihXAPzUtCwawk\n56TacQcAhkyofnwoOfak0Djv4q03vmqFev5iPigflIqDGR0Xb9iGk4fgx21W3q0u\nhCRFBVmqqYjInaG0MAhRhUAN2s6RmejKNCOWmKHA+s+64G7tFx6ZGc5B+Mgi11Jl\nms87cnuiac6B7RuNpe5el8yHcWComZS2QUGF5Prfk6WyuBVR+QfT4fISsiLYOeNL\n3aSHbESgVjM5vY5Q0A3lm5Ko4V80hwzEC+AGjzsPISszfOze0Pi9Fv5WBufOBijo\n4DWG9Caoqo8U28tWvHXWCCsKglXO7uHbOoStl7EvTtm3FkbITbrX27lTcJhBNEEG\nEOZHLsZgg9ZaS8V3CPu6CcE2A/WeF1N38C+EshmgKvzav9p+UESopxSwIiXeTYbM\ndgFUiUGl4ZUCFi01zilpQLBMJGrQeqU84GNfc81CuKRwfl6Ixu9cOe8XP0qhv5Kj\nJL74szF19hzAbtDIKV61lSx9PNeXdA2YHYWi3uyox6q5V0AYHE6Rd4qH5hvq20Bj\nby7SCssQ2IjyIkNHTUB9alDi31ih7ewvRe+IlPvcURDpQfrCdjAUwhdPqUlFV7il\nBcOHYS3AGoP/3c0FU4LD\n=UaDn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T18:20:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api