acy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/dbef560e8832c0cedf15c7424d65d7b6acd99531/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:13:33Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:13:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): stop exposing static tokens in user email and display name (#741)\n\nA static-token user''s email was static-<token>@faros.local and its display\nname \"Static Token User (<token>)\". Any member of an org or workspace the\nuser belongs to can list members and read both, which hands them a working\nbearer token. The personal org default name (\"<name>''s personal\") and the\nmembership-index rows that copy it carried the token too.\n\nStatic-token users now have no email and use their RBAC identity\n(faros:static:<hash>) as display name. Existing users are rewritten on\nlogin and by a best-effort pass at hub start, including their personal\norg''s default name and the copies of it in members'' indexes.\n\n- identity.NewStaticToken is the single derivation of sub, uid, RBAC\n  identity and User name, used by the proxy, the embedded kcp token-auth\n  file and the dev setup\n- --admin-users ignores empty entries (they would match every email-less\n  user) and warns on the retired static-<token>@faros.local form\n- faros members rejects an empty query for the same reason\n- dev admin identity, Tiltfiles, Makefile and chart docs use the RBAC\n  identity; the Makefile default was already stale","tree":{"sha":"9e7cf61f4c8dbe9690208f35dc57cdb7524b2c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/9e7cf61f4c8dbe9690208f35dc57cdb7524b2c08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/dbef560e8832c0cedf15c7424d65d7b6acd99531","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e7cf61f4c8dbe9690208f35dc57cdb7524b2c08\nparent 0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789413213 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789413213 +0300\n\nfix(auth): stop exposing static tokens in user email and display name (#741)\n\nA static-token user''s email was static-<token>@faros.local and its display\nname \"Static Token User (<token>)\". Any member of an org or workspace the\nuser belongs to can list members and read both, which hands them a working\nbearer token. The personal org default name (\"<name>''s personal\") and the\nmembership-index rows that copy it carried the token too.\n\nStatic-token users now have no email and use their RBAC identity\n(faros:static:<hash>) as display name. Existing users are rewritten on\nlogin and by a best-effort pass at hub start, including their personal\norg''s default name and the copies of it in members'' indexes.\n\n- identity.NewStaticToken is the single derivation of sub, uid, RBAC\n  identity and User name, used by the proxy, the embedded kcp token-auth\n  file and the dev setup\n- --admin-users ignores empty entries (they would match every email-less\n  user) and warns on the retired static-<token>@faros.local form\n- faros members rejects an empty query for the same reason\n- de