railgrid/railgrid/commit/dbef560e8832c0cedf15c7424d65d7b6acd99531","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKGRiZWY1NjBlODgzMmMwY2VkZjE1Yzc0MjRkNjVkN2I2YWNkOTk1MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6","sha":"0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6"}],"sha":"dbef560e8832c0cedf15c7424d65d7b6acd99531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/dbef560e8832c0cedf15c7424d65d7b6acd99531"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:02:50Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:02:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[AUTOMATED BOT PR] fix: MCP host guard, CLI unknown subcommands, provider bugs from demo apps, skill updates (#740)\n\n* fix(hub,cli): accept loopback-proxied MCP requests; fail on unknown subcommands\n\nThe MCP aggregate answered 403 \"invalid Host header\" to every request that\nreached it on a loopback socket with a non-loopback Host: hubs behind a\nsame-host proxy (cloudflared, port-forward, a sidecar) and local hubs at\nconsole.127.0.0.1.sslip.io. The go-sdk DNS-rebinding guard protects\nunauthenticated local servers; this endpoint verifies a bearer first, so the\nguard is disabled there.\n\nBelow the root, cobra printed a command group''s help and exited 0 for an\nunknown subcommand, so `faros mcp proxy` on a CLI without the proxy looked\nlike success to scripts and MCP clients. Every group now rejects unknown\narguments. docs/cli regenerated.\n\n* fix(providers): dev tool output schemas, dev_sync manifest check, token trim, edges proxy slash\n\nFound by building three demo apps against a local hub:\n\n- infrastructure: dev_sync and dev_restart did their work but returned\n  \"validating tool output: ... want one of null, array\" because the agent\n  response was a json.RawMessage, which the SDK reflects as a byte array.\n  Carry it as decoded JSON instead.\n- infrastructure: dev_sync is incremental, yet the toolchain-manifest check\n  demanded package.json in every call. Skip it for a component that already\n  has applied source or a running dev process.\n- code: trim the Connection token (and GitHub App IDs). A Secret created\n  from `gh auth token | kubectl create secret --from-file` keeps the newline\n  and net/http rejects it as an invalid Authorization header.\n- edges: \".../services/<n>/proxy\" without the trailing slash reached the\n  agent as \"/svc\", which it does not route (bare 404). Redirect a GET to a\n  relative \"proxy/\", send other methods to the service root. The\n  HostAllowed condition now names the dialed host instead of spec.host.\n\n* docs(skills): faros skill fixes from evaluation and demo-app runs\n\nOld-CLI detection for `faros mcp proxy`, the MCP host-header 403, code\nprovider readiness via readinessReason, a recipe for when git integration\nis down, template `connections` version gates, `--existing-repository`,\nWorkload targetNamespace and imagePullSecrets, the edges proxy trailing\nslash, and troubleshooting rows for the token-newline and dev tool errors.\nPlugin 0.2.1.","tree":{"sha":"cbc5fe68525e7bca4d7e341e737e0ee5dffc2224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/cbc5fe68525e7bca4d7e341e737e0ee5dffc2224"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/0c51530deed13f90305d32c1771aa9a35ed862f6","verification":{"payload":"tree cbc5fe68525e7bca4d7e341e737e0ee5dffc2224\nparent f31a50fed28d1afaa1379511a976e48f9e65a266\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789394570 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789394570 +0300\n\n[AUTOMATED BOT PR] fix: MCP host guard, CLI unknown subcommands, provider bugs from demo apps, skill updates (#740)\n\n* fix(hub,cli): accept loopback-proxied MCP requests; fail on unknown subcommands\n\nThe MCP aggregate answered 403 \"invalid Host header\" to every request that\nreached it on a loopback socket with a non-loopback Host: hubs behind a\nsame-host proxy (cloudflared, port-forward, a sidecar) and local hubs at\nconsole.127.0.0.1.sslip.io. The go-sdk DNS-rebinding guard protects\nunauthenticated local servers; this endpoint verifies a bearer first, so the\nguard is disabled there.\n\nBelow the root, cobra printed a command group''s help and exited 0 for an\nunknown subcommand, so `faros mcp proxy` on a CLI without the proxy looked\nlike success to scripts and MCP clients. Every group now rejects unknown\narguments. docs/cli regenerated.\n\n* fix(providers): dev tool output schemas, dev_sync manifest check, token trim, edges proxy slash\n\nFound by building three demo apps against a local hub:\n\n- infrastructure: dev_sync and dev_restart did their work but returned\n  \"validating tool output: ... want one of null, array\" because the agent\n  response was a json.RawMessage, which the SDK reflects as a byte array.\n  Carry it as decoded JSON instead.\n- infrastructure: dev_sync is incremental, yet the toolchain-manifest check\n  demanded package.json in every call. Skip it for a component that already\n  has applied source or a running dev process.\n- code: trim the Connection token (and GitHub App IDs). A Secret created\n  from `gh auth token | kubectl create secret --from-file` keeps the newline\n  and net/http rejects it as an invalid Authorization header.\n- edges: \".../services/<n>/proxy\" without the trailing slash reached the\n  agent as \"/svc\", which it does not route (bare 404). Redirect a GET to a\n  relative \"proxy/\", send other methods to the service root. The\n  HostAllowed condition now names the dialed host instead of spec.host.\n\n* docs(skills): faros skill fixes from evaluation and demo-app runs\n\nOld-CLI detection for `faros mcp proxy`, the MCP host-header 403, code\nprovider readiness via readinessReason, a recipe for when git integration\nis down, template `connections` version gates, `--existing-repository`,\nWorkload targetNamespace and imagePullSecrets, the edges proxy trailing\nslash, and troubleshooting rows for the token-newline and dev tool errors.\nPlugin 0.2.1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp/6KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7PkQAJN50hl00ULPqx+FiviIFpZJ\nyxCaNCVaGeMYby3C4Cd0Lk6lAqjuUo+eCQslaHo4Hz6+cKKGfqruTI1N+cizkPKy\nTCwTd4B0mvuuYn71zhfqeBk3uKNMHNNXSmSry0+DFpb5DQ2B6WBcTd+RWS+KXVU1\ntXCSzzJ8JbP5iXOJRihaAsNShuZ6SdALlY+QFHJ1lsJHWQoPaMr9bqZgtBR8MC9a\ngiXa6wdEHOffT3Ef3ludF1v55pWqxtf2rurX9gfmQsGrA8rczx8ywx8Gj9JstzOh\nZwfapfvPtOq5hIntgu5pat0Rs2Fc4aMizaEQPjKdI/B5sd1Py/eg6HOBoAUcqYgS\nE4eQu1QxUcbjh3Kkduk87lC0DSgVElFrSek1kJh8jC+xtr6P+KBGC30SR1DShcV2\nrZ5f4LBwNFUTJgKkmFl605Lt0/u9LhPEC+FKXcsrxaGxit8f8eOKGoyf/rA7Otc0\n6Jz/MkwSEAh+sHhoC8xevWNsqM3lIv5vEKZM0TxAsbFChCn0XEN3lsPLriK/v24A\nhBUTSf+72ZWILTS93xt9Jce09yHTfqVsn43vZDJkS