"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/7c19a4eef2a48482c3dac9747ae50a4bfc88fbae","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKDdjMTlhNGVlZjJhNDg0ODJjM2RhYzk3NDdhZTUwYTRiZmM4OGZiYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2","sha":"ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2"}],"sha":"7c19a4eef2a48482c3dac9747ae50a4bfc88fbae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/7c19a4eef2a48482c3dac9747ae50a4bfc88fbae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:05:08Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:05:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infrastructure): isolate tenant runtime namespaces with a NetworkPolicy (#728)\n\nThe runtime cluster is flat: a pod in one workspace can dial another\nworkspace''s Services by name (<app>-api.<clusterID>-default.svc), reaching\na private app behind its access gate, its Postgres or Redis, or a browser\ninstance. Cluster IDs are not secret.\n\nWith tenantNetworkPolicy.enabled, the Instance controller keeps an\ningress-only NetworkPolicy \"faros-tenant-isolation\" in every tenant\nruntime namespace, written before any workload. It admits pods in the\nsame namespace, the same workspace''s other runtime namespaces (by the\nprovider''s tenant + managed-by labels, backfilled on older namespaces),\nthe exposure Gateway''s namespace, and operator-listed namespaces and\nCIDRs. Egress is untouched.\n\nOff by default: the dev data plane rides the runtime apiserver''s\nservices/proxy, whose source address is topology-specific and may need\nallowedCIDRs. Turning it off removes the provider-owned policies.\n\n- chart: tenantNetworkPolicy.{enabled,allowedNamespaces,allowedCIDRs},\n  rendered as FAROS_TENANT_NETWORK_POLICY_* on the operator (copied to\n  the serve Deployment) or on the legacy serve Deployment; serve RBAC\n  gains networkpolicies and namespaces patch\n- the convergence cache is keyed by namespace UID, so a recreated\n  namespace gets its policy at once\n- CIDRs must be canonical (the apiserver rejects host bits)","tree":{"sha":"04f5714b1b461869eb314c99b66e0a1f5bc10560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/04f5714b1b461869eb314c99b66e0a1f5bc10560"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 04f5714b1b461869eb314c99b66e0a1f5bc10560\nparent a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789308308 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789308308 +0300\n\nfeat(infrastructure): isolate tenant runtime namespaces with a NetworkPolicy (#728)\n\nThe runtime cluster is flat: a pod in one workspace can dial another\nworkspace''s Services by name (<app>-api.<clusterID>-default.svc), reaching\na private app behind its access gate, its Postgres or Redis, or a browser\ninstance. Cluster IDs are not secret.\n\nWith tenantNetworkPolicy.enabled, the Instance controller keeps an\ningress-only NetworkPolicy \"faros-tenant-isolation\" in every tenant\nruntime namespace, written before any workload. It admits pods in the\nsame namespace, the same workspace''s other runtime namespaces (by the\nprovider''s tenant + managed-by labels, backfilled on older namespaces),\nthe exposure Gateway''s namespace, and operator-listed namespaces and\nCIDRs. Egress is untouched.\n\nOff by default: the dev data plane rides the runtime apiserver''s\nservices/proxy, whose source address is topology-specific and may need\nallowedCIDRs. Turning it off removes the provider-owned policies.\n\n- chart: tenantNetworkPolicy.{enabled,allowedNamespaces,allowedCIDRs},\n  rendered as FAROS_TENANT_NETWORK_POLICY_* on the operator (copied to\n  the serve Deployment) or on the legacy serve Deployment; serve RBAC\n  gains networkpolicies and namespaces patch\n- the convergence cache is keyed by namespace UID, so a recreated\n  namespace gets its policy at once\n- CIDRs must be canonical (the apiserver rejects host bits)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpq2UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlYIQAAHoMnKibuyzSpZ+EXNkKaXn\nGq0vzQAMqC6/nBNByfNB+qfQBzMHVr5KEmskRT43JXd8l7TszMUkneg0Bwyrw7Ge\nFxcRXH492LnDl2j0MGN54C5FcCFjeDgof/lBpEctckKoqBPGR4M/ZXHX6lFCleZo\nImSqmbJMWyWk3KTzSt0k0UcmuBUxqvTCJYT4WSB6hvIRZey04bTl3mFiGb4xwpMU\nSjSnoH+YfrwKKmS9+geQh6HKTBl1sa7LwSbal3hyIwj3ls7MZfIxMCZOeMAcHD8M\n+V47Qxbckjrr1P9Y10EFW5m9z6VVndeLGBw52n1+nZ/CRYAbO/mRakkm4UmH/Qyk\nIicWew90airjHwi7DYwfNkxLyumOFh41ybJeqNRoT6rEdiFe6Xuz7zHLid98dhYG\nvl9X5En0Wg5u54KoO9dZtcfMNlauchXde+Qekb7wwmEtTzqrlxL1vJxT2fwCmWqK\na5Z3wgKCmlumCp7zJ2HuiFG9bBzsxcuzFOTPxYdjUBinw2pC74/CLTKH28fzbZc/\n71/udzHbih9UAlkQ5+Bp5bpX8R3e9Ixp//pK55Hf1gj8SlqdwoJCKuNdWfUvxhiv\nomKwnGDl3pBVYLYRubTDT1viTFltKepmKStyqBIpnjef8jV2JIhCzlwno83NKU7L\nbp6SfE3B9SDCMPDWuTMQ\n=jXAe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T14:05:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKGJhN2Q1ZDRjYWZiMDIyYzJiMjc1OGQwMTY4M2YxODA1NzliZDQ3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed","sha":"a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed"}],"sha":"ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/ba7d5d4cafb022c2b2758d01683f180579bd47a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:02:21Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:02:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[AUTOMATED BOT PR] fix: field-test batch 1 (web_fetch redirects, on_request approvals, app publish/status, skill) (#726)\n\n* fix(agents): report redirects and private faros apps in web_fetch\n\nweb_fetch printed the requested URL with the final status, so a private\nfaros app that redirected to the portal sign-in page came back as\n\"HTTP 200 <app url>\" with the sign-in page as its content, and agents\nreported the app as working.\n\nIt now reports the final URL (and the URL it was redirected from), and\nstops at a redirect to /auth/apps/authorize, returning a message that the\napp is private and web_fetch cannot sign in.\n\n* fix(app-studio): require approval for promote and provision under on_request\n\npromote_project deploys to production but ran without a pause under the\ndefault on_request approval mode; only its tool description asked the\nmodel to confirm first.\n\ninfrastructure__provision was meant to pause but never did: the check\ncompared projectToolBaseName(name), which strips the provider prefix\n(\"provision\"), against the full prefixed name. It is now matched by full\nname.\n\nprepare_project_deployment is dropped from the list: it is a read-risk\ntool and only runtime-risk tools reach this check.\n\n* fix(cli): stop app publish and app status reading as failures after a change\n\n`faros app publish` printed the POST response, which is written before\nthe production instance reports the new access mode, so a working app\nshowed \"(not ready: Pending)\". It now re-reads the publishing state for\nup to 15s. A ready public publication also notes that anonymous requests\nmay still hit sign-in for about 20s.\n\n`faros app status` printed \"-  -\" for production right after a promote,\nwhile the binding status trails the instance. It now says the instance\nhas not reported yet.\n\n* skills(faros): fold in field-test round 5 and this branch''s fixes\n\nFindings from three apps built cold from the skill (a simple-webapp, an\napplication with a binary asset and an assistant turn, and an application\nwith a cron-job and a scheduled hosted agent):\n\n- Template table gains sandbox component names and where static assets\n  go; `application` has no `connections` input.\n- Machine callers: jobs and hosted agents can''t pass a private or\n  restricted app''s gate; same-workspace workloads call the app''s Service\n  directly. `restricted` and `private` are enforced the same way.\n- \"Your own secrets\": no template takes a Secret reference, and patterns\n  that work instead.\n- cron-job runs can''t be observed; how to drive a public image via env.\n- Assistant: turn status hides failed steps; the approval-mode table.\n- Smoke test on a random Postgres port, no `pkill -f`, the push guard on\n  the working clone, and `git pull --rebase` when App Studio committed.\n\nUpdated for the fixes on this branch: web_fetch now stops at a private\napp''s sign-in redirect; promote_project and infrastructure__provision\nask under on_request; `faros app publish` waits for the publication and\n`faros app status` explains an unreported production.\n\n* skills(faros): read an assistant turn''s outcome from its failure summary\n\nThe turn object now carries failedItems, recoveredItems, rejectedItems\nand failures, so the skill reads those instead of scanning every\nitem.completed event.","tree":{"sha":"b8ea8f6a0da5d1fedc258f4a600d3f593ccf3343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/b8ea8f6a0da5d1fedc258f4a600d3f593ccf3343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/a6f456ac33ccc566a3ad61bc60b34d224177f0ed","verification":{"payload":"tree b8ea8f6a0da5d1fedc258f4a600d3f593ccf3343\nparent f273ebe51d154cc9c1e09a2f9f81bfe26c14f109\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789308141 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789308141 +0300\n\n[AUTOMATED BOT PR] fix: field-test batch 1 (web_fetch redirects, on_request approvals, app publish/status, skill) (#726)\n\n* fix(agents): report redirects and private faros apps in web_fetch\n\nweb_fetch printed the requested URL with the final status, so a private\nfaros app that redirected to the portal sign-in page came back as\n\"HTTP 200 <app url>\" with the sign-in page as its content, and agents\nreported the app as working.\n\nIt now reports the final URL (and the URL it was redirected from), and\nstops at a redirect to /auth/apps/authorize, returning a message that the\napp is private and web_fetch cannot sign in.\n\n* fix(app-studio): require approval for promote and provision under on_request\n\npromote_project deploys to production but ran without a pause under the\ndefault on_request approval mode; only its tool description asked the\nmodel to confirm first.\n\ninfrastructure__provision was meant to pause but never did: the check\ncompared projectToolBaseName(name), which strips the provider prefix\n(\"provision\"), against the full prefixed name. It is now matched by full\nname.\n\nprepare_project_deployment is dropped from the list: it is a read-risk\ntool and only runtime-risk tools reach this check.\n\n* fix(cli): stop app publish and app status reading as failures after a change\n\n`faros app publish` printed the POST response, which is written before\nthe production instance reports the new access mode, so a working app\nshowed \"(not ready: Pending)\". It now re-reads the publishing state for\nup to 15s. A ready public publication also notes that anonymous requests\nmay still hit sign-in for about 20s.\n\n`faros app status` printed \"-  -\" for production right after a promote,\nwhile the binding status trails the instance. It now says the instance\nhas not reported yet.\n\n* skills(faros): fold in field-test round 5 and this branch''s fixes\n\nFindings from three apps built cold from the skill (a simple-webapp, an\napplication with a binary asset and an assistant turn, and an application\nwith a cron-job and a scheduled hosted agent):\n\n- Template table gains sandbox component names and where static assets\n  go; `application` has no `connections` input.\n- Machine callers: jobs and hosted agents can''t pass a private or\n  restricted app''s gate; same-workspace workloads call the app''s Service\n  directly. `restricted` and `private` are enforced the same way.\n- \"Your own secrets\": no template takes a Secret reference, and patterns\n  that work instead.\n- cron-job runs can''t be observed; how to drive a public image via env.\n- Assistant: turn status hides failed steps; the approval-mode table.\n- Smoke test on a random Postgres port, no `pkill -f`, the push guard on\n  the working clone, and `git pull --rebase` when App Studio committed.\n\nUpdated for the fixes on this branch: web_fetch now stops at a private\napp''s sign-in redirect; promote_project and infrastructure__provision\nask under on_request; `faros app publish` waits for the publication and\n`faros app status` explains an unreported production.\n\n* skills(faros): read an assistant turn''s outcome from its failure summary\n\nThe turn object now carries failedItems, recoveredItems, rejectedItems\nand failures, so the skill reads those instead of scanning every\nitem.completed event.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpqztCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGVQQAGBC5UaVHbq/MUs5W+72d1LJ\n0+nlQDv9LWX7jz2EdAQHoKu1UvT6+TfH1E3PrWXEmcUThxeSHcgOyWSzPcUeAEXF\n9jk83cBWlxSJDJBnUe6VKKMOtJ3T+Z1yl2eUE48n0jmIfyVX5/Jsc9EgHk8ZjDYy\nBWE03cRM0Cox0XIuAtCJlXYbZH7DQmBwTMPftZoce+MNBTiyFv53r1ZJOQnJALTn\nrn8moJAtd6BzcmFMzCvJlcdEdWG7t6EVjRGU8PTBd0D4A3N2qK50CT2du6T9vwPy\nw+4V4SgAlsh8c9v6oa0sB1y3nJ6eaU3BAuj1f90n1A7sPbKFsDaFNW+OoMr8KfyE\nZ/XEUuVRm+wEZzITZMVZ23HnhZnblc0zyGr/ZSGmz4NOlkYMmcaV+YRbaBFYXf14\nyT5Eob94F2vfxsdJd5d37Yc0Bd8/1y/E2Iq/FZg7V8+ximTlbFm4xD1uzMDnphep\nmaVvyXMpQYV+oq6M1ktnmHcz1EVyehbs7htUbTKh1OQMFNsBS5yubwc2ebPkpXrS\nOYGK4h0QV5Cbk9orpuIwo5Tk3hfTWylOwrytShiX+goehLMyRRYBpAeJO7kgmcy2\n1o7DzgL/uhLHC/QhIEvjJAKcUxdiasBvMFXxAnn3Uw71P4+EXgtfYrAOiKURcz1Z\niIXjjOAb9za+XRfOJkZk\n=Y2jU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T14:02:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/w