avatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/e138d0f90286e1f9bdfe75f5d3dfe7f17dd6adfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:33:36Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:33:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[AUTOMATED BOT PR] feat(app-studio): report failed steps on the assistant turn (#727)\n\n* feat(app-studio): report failed steps on the assistant turn\n\nA turn whose tool steps failed still ends `completed`, and the only way\nto find out was to scan every item.completed event. Field-test agents\nreported half-done work as done because of it.\n\nThe turn object in turn.completed / turn.failed / turn.interrupted\npayloads and in GET .../turns/{turn} now carries:\n\n- failedItems: tool items that ended failed\n- recoveredItems: failures a linked recoveryOf retry repaired (not failed)\n- rejectedItems: steps whose approval was denied (their items read\n  failed, but the user said no; not counted as failed)\n- failures: up to five {itemID, title, category, message, referenceID}\n  from the items'' diagnostics\n\nThe summary is derived from the turn''s durable items, so it needs no\nschema change and the detail route reports it for older turns too. All\nfields are omitted when zero; status keeps its meaning.\n\n* test(portal): match ProviderFrame''s hash-navigation watch after #720\n\n#720 made the watch callback call routeFocus.before() before\npushContext(), so the conformance regex that expected the one-liner\n`() => pushContext()` stopped matching and Root portal has failed on\nmain since. The assertion now accepts a callback block that ends in\npushContext(); it still fails if the watch stops publishing context.","tree":{"sha":"2472a0a16b5a2987d8e10e977cc6569c7944f14b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/2472a0a16b5a2987d8e10e977cc6569c7944f14b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/e138d0f90286e1f9bdfe75f5d3dfe7f17dd6adfc","verification":{"payload":"tree 2472a0a16b5a2987d8e10e977cc6569c7944f14b\nparent 0d4a624007f87addb7e86effa4c1701e448d882c\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789306416 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789306416 +0300\n\n[AUTOMATED BOT PR] feat(app-studio): report failed steps on the assistant turn (#727)\n\n* feat(app-studio): report failed steps on the assistant turn\n\nA turn whose tool steps failed still ends `completed`, and the only way\nto find out was to scan every item.completed event. Field-test agents\nreported half-done work as done because of it.\n\nThe turn object in turn.completed / turn.failed / turn.interrupted\npayloads and in GET .../turns/{turn} now carries:\n\n- failedItems: tool items that ended failed\n- recoveredItems: failures a linked recoveryOf retry repaired (not failed)\n- rejectedItems: steps whose approval was denied (their items read\n  failed, but the user said no; not counted as failed)\n- failures: up to five {itemID, title, category, message, referenceID}\n  from the items'' diagnostics\n\nThe summary is derived from the turn''s durable items, so it needs no\nschema change and the detail route reports it for older turns too. All\nfields are omitted when zero; status keeps its meaning.\n\n* test(portal): match ProviderFrame''s hash-navigation watch after #720\n\n#720 mad