29551f","sha":"c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f"}],"sha":"72392ba72fd967f29bb317fafc08037b7758f09b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/72392ba72fd967f29bb317fafc08037b7758f09b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:47:52Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:47:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[AUTOMATED BOT PR] skills(faros): CLI install guidance and in-repo plugin/Codex install (#719)\n\n* skills(faros): cover installing the CLI and working without it\n\nThe skill assumed `faros` was already on PATH and gave a one-line install\nhint that omitted the curl installer at downloads.faros.sh/install.sh.\nSection 2 now starts with a `command -v faros` check, the installer with\nits FAROS_VERSION / INSTALL_DIR knobs and PATH follow-up, the krew, go\ninstall and release-tarball alternatives with the exact asset names, and\na \"no way to install anything\" paragraph: static-token hubs log in via\nPOST /auth/token-login with curl, OIDC hubs need a service-account token\nfrom someone who has the CLI, and IDs come from GET /api/orgs.\n\naccess.md records the install paths and archive naming from install.sh\nand .goreleaser.yml; troubleshooting.md gains rows for `command not\nfound: faros`, the installer''s own errors, and the PATH miss after a\nsuccessful install.\n\n* skills(faros): install from this repo in Claude Code and Codex\n\nMake the repository itself the distribution point for the faros skill,\nwith no separate hosting:\n\n- Claude Code: a root .claude-plugin/marketplace.json declares one\n  plugin, `faros`, rooted at skills/faros, whose SKILL.md at the plugin\n  root is loaded as the single skill. Users run\n  `/plugin marketplace add faroshq/faros` and `/plugin install faros@faros`.\n  `claude plugin validate --strict` passes for both manifests and a local\n  install shows one skill, ~270 always-on tokens.\n- Codex: .agents/skills/faros is a symlink to skills/faros, the\n  repo-scoped skills directory Codex discovers, so opening the repo is\n  enough; copy the directory to ~/.agents/skills for other projects.\n\nskills/faros/README.md documents both paths plus Cursor and App Studio;\nthe top-level README lists skills/faros in the repository layout.","tree":{"sha":"296bcbe6efe8ce216bdfa338165e98a53193a4f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/296bcbe6efe8ce216bdfa338165e98a53193a4f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f","verification":{"payload":"tree 296bcbe6efe8ce216bdfa338165e98a53193a4f6\nparent d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789242472 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789242472 +0300\n\n[AUTOMATED BOT PR] skills(faros): CLI install guidance and in-repo plugin/Codex install (#719)\n\n* skills(faros): cover installing the CLI and working without it\n\nThe skill assumed `faros` was already on PATH and gave a one-line install\nhint that omitted the curl installer at downloads.faros.sh/install.sh.\nSection 2 now starts with a `command -v faros` check, the installer with\nits FAROS_VERSION / INSTALL_DIR knobs and PATH follow-up, the krew, go\ninstall and release-tarball alternatives with the exact asset names, and\na \"no way to install anything\" paragraph: static-token hubs log in via\nPOST /auth/token-login with curl, OIDC hubs need a service-account token\nfrom someone who has the CLI, and IDs come from GET /api/orgs.\n\naccess.md records the install paths and archive naming from install.sh\nand .goreleaser.yml; troubleshooting.md gains rows for `command not\nfound: faros`, the installer''s own errors, and the PATH miss after a\nsuccessful install.\n\n* skills(faros): install from this repo in Claude Code and Codex\n\nMake the repository itself the distribution point for the faros skill,\nwith no separate hosting:\n\n- Claude Code: a root .claude-plugin/marketplace.json declares one\n  plugin, `faros`, rooted at skills/faros, whose SKILL.md at the plugin\n  root is loaded as the single skill. Users run\n  `/plugin marketplace add faroshq/faros` and `/plugin install faros@faros`.\n  `claude plugin validate --strict` passes for both manifests and a local\n  install shows one skill, ~270 always-on tokens.\n- Codex: .agents/skills/faros is a symlink to skills/faros, the\n  repo-scoped skills directory Codex discovers, so opening the repo is\n  enough; copy the directory to ~/.agents/skills for other projects.\n\nskills/faros/README.md documents both paths plus Cursor and App Studio;\nthe top-level README lists skills/faros in the repository layout.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpaxoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL/0QAFuGO6grrhkSSWqhZUJbu6v7\nyU8q6zz0g5srGTd5JYhpgad9xlrw6r32IZwJf1fOqeR+mD+9pTbZY9z7MQ/7BAa5\n9i/oSv00E0q7VYOCfAVeW3WN+0nZxPHK15TyzE5bsFdX/pFSYlOuyBkHgSw/Xcsz\nTZk8EcpH61JUdTADbFgqs+UoFLfV+DvW7/NZzNG0JmuKTm1dEGDJ7sIAZLicJp4O\n+kyyAGokSnX2xbvdg69kdY79qwpE3tZiY57hJc2GcxQSHmCMLjbjfW0jNYBBisTx\n4R1BoAXTL02yOtVNmd4m3CzY7SWdAZ6BdUYhJIV8rJMs7bUrfQbeySS9nMHccedj\n9LA+Ubu9LSMViFPM6lCov6vkJW7Zn89qk3+suOCNHksJxP71wEUKFzmGdWosfm1E\njOVlApBUBWlQ/URiXKX7t39dqSf7UlJkepvOQBK2EbciJTw8C47H5FF7O2IzZlGR\nSg3htjJ8u3wwQvSRPFIFnpu95Qx5cG2hQFYG2GRdy6wtAQ2pvpqmi4cB51rggn4y\n3aFy0ch7atCs4h9imQLsdiPRa6z+oD/pKB6U8NALAEjyemPCHurVdKeTEuwxISyM\nO8AtVxQQbc6WLEZAU/Nbe2VRzYtXoEFtf6+zkmHs4VwsO1rBreYVuKBUJLE+3imr\nag3oNu/X8H0DnplKfwAX\n=IGsn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T19:47:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKGMzNjg5NTY2NjljNGQ3ZGZlNGQ5Y2RhMWY0ZDE4ZTVmMmIyOTU1MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9","sha":"d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9"}],"sha":"c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/c368956669c4d7dfe4d9cda1f4d18e5f2b29551f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:06:02Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:06:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"hub: bind org admins in every child workspace at the kcp layer (O-15) (#716)\n\nAdding or promoting an org admin only wrote the Membership CR and the\nUserMembershipIndex row. The hub side of O-15 (PR #711) then let the\nadmin through to the child workspace''s cluster, where kcp RBAC had no\nClusterRoleBinding for them and answered 403 \"access denied\".\n\nOn the way, the single shared faros-cluster-admin binding per workspace\nturned out to hold exactly one subject and be overwritten on every\ngrant, so only the last member granted actually had kcp access.\n\n- Keep one binding per user (faros-user-admin-<hash>) so grants are\n  additive; migrate the legacy shared binding to per-user bindings on\n  first touch and delete it, preserving whoever held it.\n- Add RevokeChildWorkspaceAdmin and ListOrgMembershipRoles.\n- Sync kcp RBAC on org-admin add/promote (bind everywhere), demote and\n  remove (revoke where no workspace row remains), workspace member\n  remove (revoke unless org admin) and workspace create (bind every\n  current org admin).\n- Extend the organization controller backfill to every UMI row,\n  including org-scope admin rows in other orgs, so existing state and\n  users invited before first sign-in self-heal on reconcile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a152ed9432e21579c0047920e878b2dc2824a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/3a152ed9432e21579c0047920e878b2dc2824a0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/d65dc5174899001bde930d42962190701530b3b9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a152ed9432e21579c0047920e878b2dc2824a0a\nparent 61c5b82cbc3fa0fdf8c6ecee6573451785c0b296\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789239962 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789239962 +0300\n\nhub: bind org admins in every child workspace at the kcp layer (O-15) (#716)\n\nAdding or promoting an org admin only wrote the Membership CR and the\nUserMembershipIndex row. The hub side of O-15 (PR #711) then let the\nadmin through to the child workspace''s cluster, where kcp RBAC had no\nClusterRoleBinding for them and answered 403 \"access denied\".\n\nOn the way, the single shared faros-cluster-admin binding per workspace\nturned out to hold exactly one subject and be overwritten on every\ngrant, so only the last member granted actually had kcp access.\n\n- Keep one binding per user (faros-user-admin-<hash>) so grants are\n  additive; migrate the legacy shared binding to per-user bindings on\n  first touch and delete it, preserving whoever held it.\n- Add RevokeChildWorkspaceAdmin and ListOrgMembershipRoles.\n- Sync kcp RBAC on org-admin add/promote (bind everywhere), demote and\n  remove (revoke where no workspace row remains), workspace member\n  remove (revoke unless org admin) and workspace create (bind every\n  current org admin).\n- Extend the organization controller backfill to every UMI row,\n  including org-scope admin rows in other orgs, so existing state and\n  users invited before first sign-in self-heal on reconcile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpaKaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxrQQAJyKSw5sBzgXRy95jytElZdf\nPnSuPF+taLtDj0MQCf51sULaPijZB3HSXCsa+URVkPYb1Q+2tWe5Z93mBLqd9oF6\nOQM6oj+YpBgbph2A4d0uMJCTtSex/F9WcHtQowbG0OwDqRaKIX6Wmdlov7C5AtIg\n0lZpJ9uYRsUVRXSQjlYXjaeIaisRdp8+SWUMkebx8QUoBgO1A/IItdE+PEJsWjjB\nXzfPCjKgu8hmui+S6chMyUjgVTzsxlSA6zeEaQTSbXaQjF1ivS5qMM25LxHkjcPT\noi6CNh8+RbJzH6OA7Fj/bz1IQMNl9knSdvv6qnyLHkbi1VASE2soymN59mfTU/Pa\nhV6QKBj1BYCoGcsSYug/iTXKlc8vpbwi1RwbOwfL9kQ8ic3Zkb7V3izlf0PXy5LL\nJTooVwcixwKkmh+tU/yheFeK12nJHa43YCOtAT2uQ9R9+pvdh7Nop+LsB6E3hIjM\nYkwbRaGcyoRrd3zF4Frc0QntZ38Us+b7w5ycOqnWj8rHQwXplsUbd+OFkeDtJBBa\nAvgy9u50CA/y4y1S2PFNvipk6YkJXmEYizaQHLua2cMaCDUqAXIzZz8+gGid5EIH\n/COVDp88a0Nu19XKJEYYUOoAAcXlvTfTPa+Vic+tCd9aOfjPu6AFUqbnnx2S6zGX\nWsmLv0DTz7TzQFtCAmOs\n=jWEa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T19:06:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com