:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/4ed46f67a110aecdd52621943b336df47f26ce93","node_id":"C_kwDORSHIc9oAKDRlZDQ2ZjY3YTExMGFlY2RkNTI2MjE5NDNiMzM2ZGY0N2YyNmNlOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/railgrid/railgrid/commit/4c3fe2951940d9414cbc4823b1e06f8b2feea755","sha":"4c3fe2951940d9414cbc4823b1e06f8b2feea755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/4c3fe2951940d9414cbc4823b1e06f8b2feea755"}],"sha":"4ed46f67a110aecdd52621943b336df47f26ce93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/4ed46f67a110aecdd52621943b336df47f26ce93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3225744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/4c3fe2951940d9414cbc4823b1e06f8b2feea755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:01:06Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:01:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"hub: org admins are implicit admins in every child workspace (O-15) (#711)\n\nThe tenant middleware authorized workspace-scoped requests only against\nan exact (org, workspace) UserMembershipIndex row, so an org admin added\nafter a workspace was created got 403 \"no membership found\" on every\nworkspace route — listing members, adding members, even adding\nthemselves. docs/organizations.md O-15 promises org admins implicit\nadmin in every child workspace, and the kcp proxy authorizer and the\nprovider tenant resolver already treat an org-scope row as \"the whole\norg\"; the REST middleware was the odd one out.\n\nmatchEntryOrOrgAdmin falls back to the caller''s live org-scope row for\nworkspace-scoped requests and grants admin only when that row says\nadmin. Org members still need an explicit workspace row, a soft-deleted\norg row never qualifies, and an explicit workspace row (admin or member)\nalways wins. Both Middleware and OptionalOrgMiddleware use it.\nlistWorkspaces projects admin for row-less workspaces so the portal''s\nmember-management controls render and succeed.\n\nUnit tests cover the implicit grant, explicit-row precedence, org-member\ndenial and soft-deleted org denial; the CLI e2e membership test checks\nan org admin reads a workspace roster without a row and is refused again\nafter demotion.\n\nNot covered here: org admins still get no kcp ClusterRoleBinding in\nchild workspaces (only creators and added members do), so kubectl into\nsuch a workspace needs a workspace row until that is bound.","tree":{"sha":"8e9546a9790f62a96595775426e7a143f058ee15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/8e9546a9790f62a96595775426e7a143f058ee15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/4c3fe2951940d9414cbc4823b1e06f8b2feea755","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e9546a9790f62a96595775426e7a143f058ee15\nparent 60f3130c596cf5d2e725674376a8a145a254ae58\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789236066 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789236066 +0300\n\nhub: org admins are implicit admins in every child workspace (O-15) (#711)\n\nThe tenant middleware authorized workspace-scoped requests only against\nan exact (org, workspace) UserMembershipIndex row, so an org admin added\nafter a workspace was created got 403 \"no membership found\" on every\nworkspace route — listing members, adding members, even adding\nthemselves. docs/organizations.md O-15 promises org admins implicit\nadmin in every child workspace, and the kcp proxy authorizer and the\nprovider tenant resolver already treat an org-scope row as \"the whole\norg\"; the REST middleware was the odd one out.\n\nmatchEntryOrOrgAdmin falls back to the caller''s live org-scope row for\nworkspace-scoped requests and grants admin only when that row says\nadmin. Org members still need an explicit workspace row, a soft-deleted\norg row never qualifies, and an explicit workspace row (admin or member)\nalways wins. Both Middleware and OptionalOrgMiddleware use it.\nlistWorkspaces projects admin for row-less workspaces so the portal''s\nmember-management controls render and succeed.\n\nUnit tests cover the implicit grant, explicit-row precedence, org-member\ndenial and soft-deleted org denial; the CLI e2e membership test checks\nan org admin reads a workspace roster without a row and is refused again\nafter demotion.\n\nNot covered here: org admins still get no kcp ClusterRoleBinding in\nchild workspaces (only creators and added members do), so kubectl into\nsuch a workspace needs a workspace row until that is bound.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpZNiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfpwQABoqhCFcTKX4iUsEoDKV7dM+\n+QmSM2qPVulHRwFM37CAmfdHB7omY98OKNx+KyDXX6TFluP/IT74BF67Ok3WJgok\nBgY0N3Joz6WD4lQb0y22/nKQs2ZvvGsfWtfabgp8MURmt4Y9B3XcALOcXK0DKpvH\nvOq5YH1wT5C6RMyYhg+kseyBhhQ/mOL5M1TyxB/h3r/Kx9IH584mPbTBNvX1Xj/6\nBTav9dpcaqklnOKAb4IGOzwXYVyzpJk+2sR9IG35pn9G00PO5G5sw5LaG3/lY/SF\ntYh3nnnjigicqBs8SL/z/b8uxNUqmreUgUaqQ8VIukCA2nsAG3A5s+AwIxT5lr2p\nX8/ohyvN2fiGT3rcMLJ7/wo0Xl4Ev1BjSTU4fURFqBuzvNZ0bB3GbvL+FHwarUb3\n1cN4qD6ghDCKeQPXvqyFGfGGMOIG1W58dyQDPZ601rajPvQeMFXw07eS4CZhPJi3\n5U8At1PBl+pcWmyzafPjpZVkBWTuiSTmN9XQbtDZ9NL/QiQ75SBnfENjXPp8KytK\nCe9cmAWf0rAMbgU1d47pWRmBhTzZ7BsW+s52Wx7/+1BSyGW3P5xcMV6uigMOEpm9\ny5/wuT98BkqwtZsT08lV5aDa/iNOIrzMMsfJYll4MQSdFBCbQRrkIzXkQHecTglI\nBtIih0xDMPZ1JK94t/GO\n=xrJR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T18:01:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.