rs/mjudeikis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/372e6aa4ef51c073469bdbdfc3920e59d96305be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:47:41Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:47:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[AUTOMATED BOT PR] Provider hub access as a declared, consented contract; fix workspace-admin to org-admin escalation (#709)\n\n* hub: make provider hub access part of the provider contract; fix org-admin escalation\n\nEscalation fix (pre-existing):\n- On org-scope routes the tenant middleware used the caller''s WORKSPACE role\n  whenever X-Faros-Workspace was sent, so a workspace admin (every workspace\n  creator) passed org-admin checks; adding an existing member also overwrote\n  their role. Together: any workspace admin could make themselves org admin.\n  TenantContext now carries OrgRole, requireTenantContext authorizes org\n  routes on it, and adding an existing member never changes their role\n  (roles change only through PATCH). Unit and two-user e2e regression tests.\n\nProvider hub access:\n- CatalogEntry spec.hubAccess: a provider requests capabilities from a closed,\n  hub-owned set (memberships.read org|workspace, memberships.invite org with\n  maxRole member and allowInvite). Declaring grants nothing.\n- Consent at Enable (acceptedHubAccess): org-scoped capabilities need an org\n  admin, workspace-scoped a workspace or org admin. Decisions are recorded per\n  capability (accepted / declined) in a generic Grant (tenants.faros.sh,\n  subject kind Provider) in root:faros:system:tenants; capabilities the\n  enabler may not decide keep their earlier decision or stay undecided.\n  Disable deletes the grant.\n- pkg/hub/hubaccess gate in front of the tenant routes replaces the hard-coded\n  delegated membership resolver: a delegated call is admitted only for a\n  route that maps to a capability the provider declares and the workspace\n  granted; the person''s own role still applies; handlers cap the role at\n  member and honour allowInvite; invites are rate-limited and audited.\n- Undecided capabilities fall back to --provider-hub-access-platform-default\n  (default true) for platform providers only; org-owned providers always need\n  an acceptance. Chart value hub.security.providerHubAccessPlatformDefault.\n- Delegated token proof v2 covers the provider''s owner org, so an org-owned\n  provider never uses a platform provider''s grant; v1 platform accounts are\n  re-signed in place.\n- Portal: Enable dialog lists requested capabilities with reasons; enabled\n  listing reports granted/pending; Providers page offers Review access.\n- App Studio declares the hub access it uses (manifest and chart).\n- Docs: providers.md \"Hub access\", byo-providers.md, provider-scoping.md,\n  helm.md, skill references.\n\n* Add roadmap\n\n* bump roadmap and gowork","tree":{"sha":"160c192f9a47b65255fd323108c39bf5ae586af1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/160c192f9a47b65255fd323108c39bf5ae586af1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/372e6aa4ef51c073469bdbdfc3920e59d96305be","verification":{"payload":"tree 160c192f9a47b65255fd323108c39bf5ae586af1\nparent 8e6a4e48cb0790f21b93b02d84a1c49c83f5ab2b\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789231661 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789231661 +0300\n\n[AUTOMATED BOT PR] Provider hub access as a declared, consented contract; fix workspace-admin to org-admin escalation (#709)\n\n* hub: make provider hub access part of the provider contract; fix org-admin escalation\n\nEscalation fix (pre-existing):\n- On org-scope routes the tenant middleware used the caller''s WORKSPACE role\n  whenever X-Faros-Workspace was sent, so a workspace admin (every workspace\n  creator) passed org-admin checks; adding an existing member also overwrote\n  their role. Together: any workspace admin could make themselves org admin.\n  TenantContext now carries OrgRole, requireTenantContext authorizes org\n  routes on it, and adding an existing member never changes their role\n  (roles change only through PATCH). Unit and two-user e2e regression tests.\n\nProvider hub access:\n- CatalogEntry spec.hubAccess: a provider requests capabilities from a closed,\n  hub-owned set (memberships.read org|workspace, memberships.invite org with\n  maxRole member and allowInvite). Declaring grants nothing.\n- Consent at Enable (acceptedHubAccess): org-scoped capabilities need an org\n  admin, workspace-scoped a workspace or org admin. Decisions are recorded per\n  capability (accepted / declined) in a generic Grant (tenants.faros.sh,\n  subject kind Provider) in root:faros:system:tenants; capabilities the\n  enabler may not decide keep their earlier decision or stay undecided.\n  Disable deletes the grant.\n- pkg/hub/hubaccess gate in front of the tenant routes replaces the hard-coded\n  delegated membership resolver: a delegated call is admitted only for a\n  route that maps to a capability the provider declares and the workspace\n  granted; the person''s own role still applies; handlers cap the role at\n  member and honour allowInvite; invites are rate-limited and audited.\n- Undecided capabilities fall back to --provider-hub-access-platform-default\n  (default true) for platform providers only; org-owned providers always need\n  an acceptance. Chart value hub.security.providerHubAccessPlatformDefault.\n- Delegated token proof v2 covers the provider''s owner org, so an org-owned\n  provider never uses a platform provider''s grant; v1 platform accounts are\n  re-signed in place.\n- Portal: Enable dialog lists requested capabilities with reasons; enabled\n  listing reports granted/pending; Providers page offers Review access.\n- App Studio declares the hub access it uses (manifest and chart).\n- Docs: providers.md \"Hub access\", byo-providers.md, provider-scoping.md,\n  helm.md, skill references.\n\n* Add roadmap\n\n* bump roadmap and gowork","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpYItCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmG0QAIHR5o1KV8cAe2rLXLYraQd6\nJu/gB6WjWYhTKaMxCT8EKjahU+FCNrwHiIhKTG35KfGUQskwEnVK2YzYt4x1zLwO\nC9yqEBahOmmfPxAZmp4OIPa+VdELt0fc4rV2Ty748zCAh1Ut7zIBhZlKK28FYB3j\nl33x/QmESF7Ea+Vss3LYHnUUsU2ZJt7+q46PepczFxXydRUKunyAAdmNLuSlkIUy\nr0FnHp6IwiUIKHjd6AbGvMjh4OVEAas0L/YUNS9XFDp3edFZsMLGJPX3Uz0h2tOf\nMj0qXiiLul0766Z3up6d8L6p2DbMU1iLPD0sdsmU6nZ9jv2gJCZ4yHQAO9+kJSE7\nZVMYzzOI3dEqemGJqxQWazDJQEwrn65jLXrPu0PO0faL1Nra1Is4wiI7E5efKBGp\nhQ1Nacl5E81i+doxE3/w/RcE8s2mptO6rXmSD7++spfiKsGCRTaSzbHO3OXGf5Mz\nUnbo4XmDtjOb/BUY+VL59jM8Z6YJIfi55K6AVL5SUvJhXiJDvQE5XOizJFx+v0oj\nJjd+3qxPok127lAUEyIrq8cSDbFoubtN6KYVXKkcbyrUsVr26ZIm2ILnIWBLp1x0\nfMETDqH7ikGM9R8+5HoQdLt5KJI1o/f2rkvmNMbrAisgiH4Hiusgk1AOVadO+M4T\nMuInfVFPvqbLySZ3rl7N\n=FFko\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T16:47:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com