://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mjudeikis","id":3225744,"login":"mjudeikis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjU3NDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjudeikis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/commits/d7329ee9fa7a4c6021c5ba5ae66abec56e742db3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:05:36Z","email":"mangirdas@judeikis.lt","name":"Mangirdas Judeikis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:05:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(kuery-portal): keep the Force topology layout off the main thread (#699)\n\nSelecting the \"Force\" layout in the fleet topology view froze the tab\nfor minutes on a real fleet (two edges, ~2,000 members): the portal\nlooked as if the provider had gone down, then came back when the\nlayout finished. The provider was fine — every topology query answered\nin ~100 ms — the cost was Cytoscape''s cose layout run with\nanimate:false, which executes all iterations (O(nodes²) each, 1,000 of\nthem) in one synchronous loop.\n\n- graph.ts: forceLayoutSizing/forceLayoutOptions size cose to the\n  graph: animate across frames above 120 nodes (Cytoscape runs\n  `refresh` iterations per animation frame, so the page stays\n  interactive), fewer iterations on big graphs under a fixed work\n  budget, a cooling schedule that still converges within that budget,\n  and few iterations per frame so frames stay short. A fresh graph is\n  randomized; relayouts start from current positions.\n- mountGraph tracks one layout at a time: the initial layout goes\n  through the same path, a relayout stops a still-running layout\n  first, destroy stops it, and a hook reports activity to the view.\n  relayout now resolves on layoutstop.\n- TopologyView: uses the sized force layout, shows that the layout is\n  settling with a Stop layout control, and runs the force layout once\n  after Expand all instead of every three rounds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6387e7b19ba1c7bdadaa55d33555dc381dbb9a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/trees/f6387e7b19ba1c7bdadaa55d33555dc381dbb9a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/railgrid/railgrid/git/commits/d7329ee9fa7a4c6021c5ba5ae66abec56e742db3","verification":{"payload":"tree f6387e7b19ba1c7bdadaa55d33555dc381dbb9a8\nparent 429ed15dc5026879238582081485fae13b024b9a\nauthor Mangirdas Judeikis <mangirdas@judeikis.lt> 1789229136 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789229136 +0300\n\nperf(kuery-portal): keep the Force topology layout off the main thread (#699)\n\nSelecting the \"Force\" layout in the fleet topology view froze the tab\nfor minutes on a real fleet (two edges, ~2,000 members): the portal\nlooked as if the provider had gone down, then came back when the\nlayout finished. The provider was fine — every topology query answered\nin ~100 ms — the cost was Cytoscape''s cose layout run with\nanimate:false, which executes all iterations (O(nodes²) each, 1,000 of\nthem) in one synchronous loop.\n\n- graph.ts: forceLayoutSizing/forceLayoutOptions size cose to the\n  graph: animate across frames above 120 nodes (Cytoscape runs\n  `refresh` iterations per animation frame, so the page stays\n  interactive), fewer iterations on big graphs under a fixed work\n  budget, a cooling schedule that still converges within that budget,\n  and few iterations per frame so frames stay short. A fresh graph is\n  randomized; relayouts start from current positions.\n- mountGraph tracks one layout at a time: the initial layout goes\n  through the same path, a relayout stops a still-running layout\n  first, destroy stops it, and a hook reports activity to the view.\n  relayout now resolves on layoutstop.\n- TopologyView: uses the sized force layout, shows that the layout is\n  settling with a Stop layout control, and runs the force layout once\n  after Expand all instead of every three rounds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpXhQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbOcQAGYRH/3oLMir9Hrpi/JLyv2b\nofYOSf6UsN37Ve3mmZuHNH94+BEhK/Pfqm4AZocMl0IvITjfwb+HLlr3k4Lg/fVG\nBk1EZLIaRnXBlBkDMQ4AmutBqUvmOxI7R0C62ZMoGLf+pr9/J4G0AzYvvBckf1kW\nKODJwU+fgKqZ7xSnF/xUcamKUWbk7THLPvH+nJSoiQDIl7IlFI21wLjZo1ZrHSAt\nuJlDNgh4UmWdOzTanGYjcYuyGlb5ShCY7v6c8tf4ByBBz/rA9KRpoDdV0nk1enPW\nzUMGRX/ApOfjAMoCSrCW9ibcAEbugogiTb7Y/ot2sgqPKN2LUf2f+jueynCc8YHK\nR3OvydcGn+WB4cSzzZENtCQ8oSpkdNV0ryAJq0WW1OiEvYSg1xZFlMfRGQxcpx7X\n3tJ9IvnTgj2F7WwxsR0aM6fuK/nIIhSOKj8EJGADhbl9GM3Gx2lmL8DrGEO70ylX\nFesM/JG9pgS9yNPIbr/CXjrA/VeityrI5ZEEmUoWP+N70yRCugGgOEFtrN05kW6y\nW/HH0+is1sOTVf7iXh7gaViH+QzC8wQN2YsjVrq5A3BTFAI5RB/4ku5GK2CxiV4F\nBiV44t+9Q89LD0CJzQMZBrfYWDaQgZE0Z9bbRoHpOj2KmzaQ/vLKQ57r5d6PZOzc\no8nS3qFfvACOYmH4nYzh\n=k4Ly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T16:05:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow