triggers refetches when\nmutations complete, without requiring RTK Query tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3f371a2668a1a346c53f7eec97b3d1a3d93e28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/esanmohammad/Micro-Frontend-API-caching/git/trees/e3f371a2668a1a346c53f7eec97b3d1a3d93e28b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/esanmohammad/Micro-Frontend-API-caching/git/commits/b5213271754935c0bb4d5de9bfd275125366b080","verification":{"payload":"tree e3f371a2668a1a346c53f7eec97b3d1a3d93e28b\nparent c2984d73e6e1e55061b95245936f5fb27a9a4e01\nauthor Esan Mohammad <esan.mohammad@sendinblue.com> 1771329974 +0530\ncommitter Esan Mohammad <esan.mohammad@sendinblue.com> 1771329974 +0530\n\nfix(dtsl-rtk-query): fix URL-based auto-invalidation for mutations\n\n- Extract mutation URL from baseQueryMeta.request.url instead of\n  originalArgs, fixing mutations where args is just an ID (not URL object)\n- Extract HTTP method from request metadata for accurate detection\n- Register queries with full URL path (including baseUrl prefix) so\n  query paths match mutation paths for invalidation matching\n- Clean up debug logs, use debug flag for optional logging\n\nThe URL-based invalidation now correctly triggers refetches when\nmutations complete, without requiring RTK Query tags.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQA3PJr12+dDwNdm5CBzld5BA1TGgUCaZRZtwAKCRCBzld5BA1T\nGhxlAP9xu0kMtAfgXTi6Ni4XcRt6INPfDmvgGskYIeJAprR8EAD/UwgGclutITIV\nFycvrvx7523N+4Om32yfsgxJUifwpgs=\n=Oxv5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-17T12:08:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117162150?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esanmohammad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esanmohammad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esanmohammad/following{/other_