kend/feature magic link auth (#9)\n\n* feat: Multi-method auth architecture - Phase 1 (DB schema, Email/Password, Email OTP)\n\n- Step 0: DB Schema\n  - Added AuthIdentity model for multi-provider auth support\n  - Added VerificationCode model for OTP and magic link tokens\n  - Added backfill script for migrating existing users\n  - Migration pending (requires DB connection)\n\n- Method 1: Email/Password (refined)\n  - Refactored to use AuthIdentity for user lookup\n  - Config-driven route mounting\n  - Updated tests (5 tests passing)\n\n- Method 2: Email OTP (complete E2E)\n  - OTP send handler with email integration\n  - OTP verify handler with JWT issuance\n  - VerificationCode repository\n  - All tests passing (18 tests)\n  - Swagger documentation\n  - Postman collection\n\n- Infrastructure\n  - Auth config loader (mirrors frontend auth.json)\n  - Email service abstraction (nodemailer/SendGrid/console)\n  - Config-driven method enable/disable\n  - Developer guide and setup documentation\n\n- Email Service\n  - Free SMTP support (Gmail, Outlook)\n  - SendGrid adapter ready for future use\n  - Console provider for development\n  - Comprehensive documentation\n\nFiles:\n- New: auth-identity.repository.ts, verification-code.repository.ts\n- New: email.service.ts, auth-config.loader.ts\n- New: otp-send.handler.ts, otp-verify.handler.ts\n- New: Documentation (DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md, EMAIL_SERVICE.md, etc.)\n- New: Postman collection, backfill script\n- Modified: login.handler.ts, routes.ts, schema.prisma, package.json\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: Add migration run guide clarifying local/server execution\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: Update migration guide with local execution details\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add database seed script for development and testing\n\n- Creates sample tenants (acme-corp, demo-company)\n- Creates roles (USER, ADMIN, OWNER)\n- Creates 4 test users with passwords\n- Creates AuthIdentity records for all users\n- Links users to tenants with role assignments\n- Idempotent (safe to run multiple times)\n- Includes seed guide documentation\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* fix: Configure Prisma migrations to load .env.local via dotenv-cli\n\n- Updated db:migrate script to use dotenv-cli\n- Added dotenv-cli as dev dependency\n- Added ENV_FILE_SETUP.md guide explaining .env.local loading\n- Fixes DIRECT_URL not found error when using .env.local\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add Magic Link authentication method (Method 3)\n\n- Implement send magic link handler with secure token generation\n- Implement verify magic link handler with GET/POST support\n- Add config-driven route mounting for magic_link method\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (13 tests, all passing)\n- Add Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- Update Postman collection with Magic Link requests\n- Update Developer Guide with Method 3 documentation\n\nFeatures:\n- Secure 32-byte random token generation\n- Token hashing and storage in VerificationCode table\n- Email sending via email service abstraction\n- Support for browser redirect (GET) and API (POST) verification\n- Configurable expiry, signup allowance, and domain restrictions\n- Development mode returns magic link URL for testing\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* security: Remove exposed secrets from ENV_FILE_SETUP.md\n\n- Replace actual Supabase project reference with [PROJECT_REF] placeholder\n- Replace actual password with [PASSWORD] placeholder\n- Add example with placeholder values instead of real credentials\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* chore: Trigger GitGuardian rescan after security fix\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add Phone OTP authentication method (Method 4)\n\n- Implement send phone OTP handler with E.164 phone validation\n- Implement verify phone OTP handler with JWT issuance\n- Add SMS service abstraction (Twilio/Console providers)\n- Add config-driven route mounting for phone_sms_otp method\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (15 tests, all passing)\n- Add Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- Update Postman collection with Phone OTP requests\n- Update Developer Guide with Method 4 documentation\n- Add SMS_SERVICE.md documentation\n\nFeatures:\n- E.164 phone number format validation and normalization\n- Automatic normalization of 10-digit US numbers to +1XXXXXXXXXX\n- SMS service abstraction (Twilio for production, Console for dev)\n- OTP code hashing and storage in VerificationCode table\n- Configurable expiry, max attempts, and sender number\n- Development mode returns OTP code in response for testing\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add OAuth authentication method (Method 5)\n\n- Implement OAuth service abstraction (Google, GitHub, Microsoft)\n- Implement OAuth initiation handler with CSRF state protection\n- Implement OAuth callback handler with account linking\n- Add config-driven route mounting for oauth method\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (15 tests, all passing)\n- Add Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- Update Postman collection with OAuth requests\n- Update Developer Guide with Method 5 documentation\n- Update user repository to support null passwordHash for OAuth signup\n\nFeatures:\n- OAuth2/OIDC flow with multiple providers (Google, GitHub, Microsoft)\n- CSRF protection via state parameter (stored in httpOnly cookie)\n- Account linking (link OAuth to existing users by email)\n- Automatic user creation for new OAuth accounts\n- Provider-specific user info normalization\n- GitHub email fetching from emails endpoint when needed\n- Redirect support for post-login navigation\n- Configurable allowSignup and allowLinking\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add support for 12 additional OAuth providers\n\nAdded provider support for:\n- Facebook, Twitter/X, Apple, Discord, LinkedIn, Slack\n- Spotify, Twitch, GitLab, Bitbucket, Dropbox, Reddit, Zoom\n\nTotal: 15 OAuth providers (3 existing + 12 new)\n\nChanges:\n- Extended oauth.service.ts with 12 new provider configurations\n- Added normalization logic for each provider''s user info structure\n- Added provider-specific handling (Slack token response, Twitch Client-Id header, etc.)\n- Updated .env.example with all provider environment variables\n- Created documentation (OAUTH_PROVIDERS.md, BETTER_AUTH_INTEGRATION_ANALYSIS.md)\n\nProvider-specific features:\n- Twitter: Handles API v2 nested data structure\n- Apple: Ready for JWT ID token handling\n- Discord: Constructs avatar URL from avatar hash\n- Slack: Handles user info in token response\n- Twitch: Requires Client-Id header for user info\n- Bitbucket: Handles nested links structure\n- Reddit: Handles optional email field\n\nAll providers follow the same OAuth2/OIDC flow pattern and can be enabled via auth.json config.\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: Update METHOD_STATUS.md to reflect all 15 OAuth providers\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* fix: Correct OAuth provider count to 16 (was incorrectly listed as 15)\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Complete Phase 1 - Add rate limiting, account recovery, MFA, session enhancements, and documentation\n\n- Add rate limiting middleware (config-driven from auth.json)\n- Add password reset functionality (request and complete)\n- Add MFA support (TOTP with QR codes and backup codes)\n- Enhance session management (config-driven cookies, remember me)\n- Add Swagger documentation for all new endpoints\n- Add unit tests for password reset handlers\n- Update Developer Guide with all new features\n- Create Phase 2 roadmap (WebAuthn, SSO)\n- Create logging and monitori