o for production, Console for dev)\n- OTP code hashing and storage in VerificationCode table\n- Configurable expiry, max attempts, and sender number\n- Development mode returns OTP code in response for testing\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add OAuth authentication method (Method 5)\n\n- Implement OAuth service abstraction (Google, GitHub, Microsoft)\n- Implement OAuth initiation handler with CSRF state protection\n- Implement OAuth callback handler with account linking\n- Add config-driven route mounting for oauth method\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (15 tests, all passing)\n- Add Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- Update Postman collection with OAuth requests\n- Update Developer Guide with Method 5 documentation\n- Update user repository to support null passwordHash for OAuth signup\n\nFeatures:\n- OAuth2/OIDC flow with multiple providers (Google, GitHub, Microsoft)\n- CSRF protection via state parameter (stored in httpOnly cookie)\n- Account linking (link OAuth to existing users by email)\n- Automatic user creation for new OAuth accounts\n- Provider-specific user info normalization\n- GitHub email fetching from emails endpoint when needed\n- Redirect support for post-login navigation\n- Configurable allowSignup and allowLinking\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Add support for 12 additional OAuth providers\n\nAdded provider support for:\n- Facebook, Twitter/X, Apple, Discord, LinkedIn, Slack\n- Spotify, Twitch, GitLab, Bitbucket, Dropbox, Reddit, Zoom\n\nTotal: 15 OAuth providers (3 existing + 12 new)\n\nChanges:\n- Extended oauth.service.ts with 12 new provider configurations\n- Added normalization logic for each provider''s user info structure\n- Added provider-specific handling (Slack token response, Twitch Client-Id header, etc.)\n- Updated .env.example with all provider environment variables\n- Created documentation (OAUTH_PROVIDERS.md, BETTER_AUTH_INTEGRATION_ANALYSIS.md)\n\nProvider-specific features:\n- Twitter: Handles API v2 nested data structure\n- Apple: Ready for JWT ID token handling\n- Discord: Constructs avatar URL from avatar hash\n- Slack: Handles user info in token response\n- Twitch: Requires Client-Id header for user info\n- Bitbucket: Handles nested links structure\n- Reddit: Handles optional email field\n\nAll providers follow the same OAuth2/OIDC flow pattern and can be enabled via auth.json config.\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: Update METHOD_STATUS.md to reflect all 15 OAuth providers\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* fix: Correct OAuth provider count to 16 (was incorrectly listed as 15)\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* feat: Complete Phase 1 - Add rate limiting, account recovery, MFA, session enhancements, and documentation\n\n- Add rate limiting middleware (config-driven from auth.json)\n- Add password reset functionality (request and complete)\n- Add MFA support (TOTP with QR codes and backup codes)\n- Enhance session management (config-driven cookies, remember me)\n- Add Swagger documentation for all new endpoints\n- Add unit tests for password reset handlers\n- Update Developer Guide with all new features\n- Create Phase 2 roadmap (WebAuthn, SSO)\n- Create logging and monitoring plan\n- Add completion summary document\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* test: Add comprehensive MFA unit tests and update Postman collection\n\n- Add 30 MFA unit tests (enable, verify-setup, verify, disable handlers)\n- Fix password reset tests with proper mocks\n- Update Postman collection with password reset endpoints\n- Update Postman collection with MFA endpoints (enable, verify-setup, verify, disable)\n- Add Postman variables for MFA and password reset\n- All 41 new tests passing ✅\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: Add Phase 2 roadmap document to screen architecture & designs folder\n\nCo-authored-by: mohapatra.dev02 <mohapatra.dev02@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpreZLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA//0QAHBMCdu51A99ILp9yKDqf7M9\nlUmRKpSSyo0BSWAikHeJEfyyfz5NHqAXO0Z1I6oDD7iSNK2Xi1OqJYghJjSiy4wm\nP+cvTis45xPRerV939DgKFEYZZUwGjJlSHVtthkG4a6lvyH323llsl8IB2t/carR\nXWSMVkYFHwC/0g3cujMkjerh3kAhwxWxvI4Dk/kQcBYoTm+P09CXHRFNlWE4Zu6G\nD6x/02zqcZrd55rIKCsugCURXX+ybh49DO9/PNsAEanyOt3XQmpQykfNnGSxADBw\nbn/14PecvIecksOI9pbrHJd/tTGQ0SXAX1g4knjGCaWlbSiF7LRGw6tl+TXbRbd8\nmSniEZZ7S88DOTHF6C1Z3Y5TFmf+740vz/+71yHo+dmBzBSb6SErqfIlboyRav1X\nDBiwCLmm3BfwfD5YzzbRJ40VgyEeGnAGoPls9qcwX/IgyCL7HhcK4eIah911QzAg\nvOZfyNZvHrvP5dUGSyHOm/IO3nCLHAUvn43EsrQ74qaHRKTBEewFLzpps58O2Bfm\nfOGbl8h3aZBWkjU2iC7411kEtE5K0qLoWJd4iQ5arcIILo07khgRsaoR+Sx558qJ\n1952VfJzP8vR/fFkeSpDAGXabykJZlY3kJi2LtLtTXi8NcWqoX1cK8GxDaXCjVMn\n2Jsfifcjq9VTnlZD1aO6\n=2433\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-08T21:12:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_v